how to make a website  if you don't know anything about  websites okay if you're starting a  business  and you don't know about the product  category that you're getting into  you have to find a way to either learn  it yourself or better yet  bring people on board who can help you  okay this comes as a response to  question i got from one of my youtube  viewers jim jones  who wrote in to say i have a question uh  i want to make a micro blogging site my  target market is age 14 and above i'm  currently struggling to find the funding  and right people to help me realize this  dream  as unfortunately i'm not a programmer  what do i do  so jim here's the thing okay if you want  to have a lot of success in this field  it's probably not going to be by you  becoming  a programmer okay that that might help  but if you're not interested in  programming if you're not passionate  about being a programmer  it's not going to work it's going to be  a mediocre product  so you got to think what are you really  good at and then bring people on board  who can support you  the two ways to do it here if you're  building technology product  you need to have somebody on board who  gets technology that's a big thing  that's kind of a big deal right so you  have to find that person  the two ways to do it is one you hire  them and at a startup you don't have a  lot of money to do it  right if you've got tons of backing  that's one thing but you probably don't  have a ton of cash  most of the best startups in the  technology space we're started by people  who get  technology so you need to find the  person who gets technology to guide you  along the way here  the way to do it is find someone who you  can partner up with  find someone who believes the same thing  that you believe in  but doesn't have your skills they have  the technology skills  they want to build the exact same thing  but they have no idea how to  build a company and how to market this  that's where you come in  hopefully i don't know where you come in  you got to tell me what you're good at  hopefully you're good at something that  relates to this and go find that person  how do you find that person you have to  hang around in the circles that relate  to what you're talking about  so here's here's an example let me bring  this home for you in a tangible example  okay  uh i've got a guy who's helping me now  my team named jason  and jason has done a lot of great work  on the branding the design  a lot of the thinking behind the the  business and the website  and taking in the direction that that i  wasn't thinking of before and i didn't  have the skills for  how did i find jason okay  there was an event here in toronto that  i created uh a  coffee shop that i really liked a bus  ran into that coffee shop and the owner  had to close down for a few days can you  imagine a bus  hitting your store like it's hard enough  to be an entrepreneur and here comes  this bus that plows through your front  door so they had to shut down while they  built the front of their store back up  and when they opened up again  i put out a note to my newsletter list  to say  hey guys here's what happened to the  store little nicki's  i want to go surprise them one day and  just  buy their stuff grab some coffee meet  you entrepreneurs and talk business and  support this entrepreneur  why did i do this because i believe in  entrepreneurs that's what i do i love  entrepreneurs  everything i do is about  entrepreneurship and the people on my  team have to love entrepreneurs too  so when i went to that event i met jason  there  it's the first time i met him in person  and we we hit it off and nothing  happened right away we didn't have an  idea to work together on something right  away but over time things developed and  we hit it off  and it worked well because we believed  in the same thing  but we had different skill sets and we  found  each other by going to events that  related to what we believed in  so this thing that you're trying to  build who's it going to help  how is it going to help them why is this  important like this has to mean  something to you  and start going to events or create your  own event  that relate to that topic if it was  around entrepreneurship for me i would  create an entrepreneurship event i would  go  to any entrepreneur event here in my  city or conference that i wanted to  learn about  i would go there because the people  there they like the same thing  they believe the same thing that i do  but they have different skills  and that means partnership opportunities  okay you got to find that person if you  want to build a successful  technology-based company  you need somebody who gets technology  you're not going to get funding without  that person you said you're trying to  get funded you go to banks you go to  investors you go to angels vcs whoever  it is  nobody's going to give you money if  you're a technology company  without the technology person so you  either have to find that person  or take your company in a different  direction that doesn't rely on  technology  where you can use your strengths and you  don't need the partners  those are your options great question  believe  those are watching like the video give  it a thumbs up below make sure to do  more  and let me know what you think leave a  comment below you have a question put it  below make a video response  thank you so much and i'll see you soon

